# RealmForge Cline Instructions — Mandatory Skill Enforcement

This file is the gatekeeper. Every session, every action, every tool invocation
in this workspace is governed by the RealmForge skill system. Nothing happens
without a skill.

## ⚠️ ABSOLUTE RULES

### 1. No Action Without a Skill

You MUST NOT perform any productive work — including reading code, writing code,
running tools, making decisions, or answering questions — without first:

1. Identifying which RealmForge skill owns the domain (see `.clinerules/02-routing-and-skills.md`)
2. Loading that skill using `use_skill` with the exact skill name
3. Following the skill's workflow instructions

This includes:
- Writing or editing Rust code
- Creating or editing documentation
- Running tests or builds
- Making architectural decisions
- Planning or scoping work
- Reviewing code or specs
- Writing ADRs or API docs
- Any financial analysis or cost modeling
- Any security review or threat modeling
- Any deployment or release decisions
- Any user-facing requirement definition

### 2. Session Start Protocol

Every new session MUST begin with this sequence BEFORE any tools are used:

```
1. Read .clinerules/00-company-index.md     — know the company skill deck
2. Read .clinerules/01-session-protocol.md  — follow session protocol
3. Read .clinerules/02-routing-and-skills.md — match request to skill
4. Read .clinerules/03-docs-first-law.md — enforce specs, metadata, work paths, grants, and tests
5. Read .clinerules/04-architecture-laws.md — enforce layer law, crate law, and Rust rules
6. Read .clinerules/05-workflow-and-handoffs.md — enforce handoff discipline
7. Read .clinerules/06-repo-hygiene-and-verification.md — keep repo/docs clean
8. Read .clinerules/07-focused-workflow-lifecycle.md — follow Idea → Planning → Architecture → Development → Testing → Documentation
9. Use_skill to load the matching skill      — adopt persona and workflow
```

### 3. No Bypassing the Handoff Chain

Work must flow through: CEO → PM → CTO → Architects (as needed) → Engineering → Peer Review → Code Review → QA → Release Manager.
Direct engineering-to-release without QA is a violation.
Direct engineering-to-deployment without Release Manager is a violation.
Any handoff must have a named deliverable and a named receiver.

